Ticket **#4471** is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. The export says otherwise.
Its reports hold two causes, and the fix covers only the first. Every number below is
computed from the export at render time — the same logic the desk runs in
`causes.ts`, not intake's guess.

<Callout kind="warn">
Two causes. The fix queued for #4471 covers only one of them.
</Callout>

## What the merged reports hold

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table groups the ticket's unique reports (one id, one report) by cause, from each
tenant's locale and booking form — never from `meta.intakeTag`, which is intake's guess
from the reporter's browser and disagrees with the real cause for a chunk of reports.

## The two problems

**`parser` — the one the fix covers.** The shared parser reads every date month first.
Every tenant on file writes the day first, so their dates come out flipped. All tenants,
every channel except booking-v3's form. This is the cause #4471 was merged for, and the
queued fix is for it.

**`hint` — the one without a ticket.** The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its
date field. The tenant's people type what the hint tells them, month first, and the form
then reads what they typed the tenant's way, day first. A second flip, in the form's own
field, before the shared parser is ever reached. Only the booking-v3 tenants, only
reports that arrived through the form. Merged into #4471 by subject like everything else,
so it sits inside a ticket marked known — when the queued fix ships, these reports keep
coming in.

## What the desk read differently

The reports the desk read as a one-day move are counted where they were filed and
footnoted under their cause (`desk-notes.json`), as the table shows. They change no count
on this page.

## Where the counts went

One issue per cause is filed in the public repo for this split,
[philipschm1tt/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows](https://github.com/philipschm1tt/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows),
each with the count of reports it covers. `parser` also keeps its place as #4471 in the
ticket system; `hint` needs its own ticket there, and its own fix.

A big ticket is not always one bug. Merge early, but group by cause before the count is
spent on a single fix.

